 succeeded in 0ms:
31:class ServerRequestContext(Generic[LifespanContextT, RequestT]):
   160	    The method and the raw inbound params are `ctx.method` and `ctx.params` (no
   161	    model validation has happened yet). To rewrite either before the handler
   162	    runs, pass an adjusted context: `await call_next(replace(ctx, params=...))`.
   163	    `ctx.request_id is None` distinguishes a notification from a request. For
   164	    notifications `call_next(ctx)` returns `None` (a dropped or unhandled
   165	    notification also returns `None`) and the middleware's own return value is
   166	    discarded.
   167	
   168	    !!! warning
   169	        `initialize` is handled inline - the dispatcher does not read
   170	        further inbound messages until the middleware chain returns. Awaiting a
   171	        server-to-client request (`ctx.session.send_request`, `send_ping`, ...)
   172	        while handling `initialize` therefore deadlocks the connection: the
   173	        response can never be dequeued. Send-and-forget notifications are safe.
   174	        `initialize` is observed but not rewritable: the post-chain handshake
   175	        commit reads the wire params, so to veto the handshake raise *before*
   176	        `call_next()`.
